BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Vallejo Swings! The music of Duke Ellington with Nick Rossi's Jazz
 opaters
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260711T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260711T220000
UID:260708_MIXRE7QyEW6Vy68g3MrVA
DESCRIPTION:One night only: a very special Saturday night music and dance 
 event with Nick Rossi's Jazzopaters making their Vallejo debut playing the
  compositions/arrangements of the maestro\, Duke Ellington! Come enjoy two
  sets of Swing Era Ellingtonia performed by this fantastic 9-piece band\, 
 the only ensemble of its kind west of the Continental Divide. The historic
  Odd Fellows Hall\, located downtown on Georgia Street\, welcomes this spe
 cial little big band to its Grand Ballroom. Both the dance floor and bar w
 ill be open. You can catch the group hot on their heels of their sold out 
 appearance down south at the Stanford Jazz Workshop the night before.\n\nC
 onfirmed personnel: Patrick Wolff\, alto sax & clarinet\; Nathan Tokunaga\
 , clarinet\, tenor sax\, & soprano sax\; Kamrin Ortiz\, baritone sax & cla
 rinet\; James Dunning\, trumpet\; Victor Imbo\, trombone\; Adam Shulman\, 
 piano\; Nick Rossi\, guitar\; Mikiya Matsuda\, bass\; Riley Baker\, drums.
 \n\n$20 \\(plus online booking fee\\) advance tickets highly recommended\,
  but tickets will be available at the door \\(cash or Venmo preferred\\). 
 Additional donations to the band/project gratefully accepted via PayPal \\
 (nickrossimusic@gmail.com\\) and Venmo \\(@nickrossimusic\\). Tickets are 
 non-refundable but fully transferable.\n\nHistoric note: Duke Ellington an
 d his Famous Orchestra performed in Vallejo once. On the evening of Monday
 \, June 19\, 1942\, the band appeared at Casa de Vallejo on Sonoma Bouleva
 rd and while the building still stands\, live music long ago stopped being
  featured there. This performance is in part a commemoration of Duke's fir
 st and only appearance in Vallejo.
LOCATION:Odd Fellows Hall
URL:https://www.tickettailor.com/events/nickrossimusic/2294969
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
