DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260711T163000
UID:260701ida0gvOaukmcd60NxGlkqw
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an inspiring afternoon at the Petaluma Arts Center
  for Teaching As Art Practice\, a panel discussion exploring the dynamic r
 elationship between teaching and creative practice.\n\nDrawing from Aristo
 tle's quote\, &ldquo\;Those who can\, do\; those who understand\, teach\,&
 rdquo\; this conversation brings together artist educators from across the
  North Bay to discuss how teaching art shapes\, challenges\, and enriches 
 their own artistic work. Through personal experiences and shared perspecti
 ves\, panelists will reflect on mentorship\, creative process\, pedagogy\,
  and the evolving role of educators within contemporary art communities.\n
 \nThe panel features professors and teachers from Sonoma State University\
 , College of Marin\, and Santa Rosa Junior College.\n\nModerated by New Vo
 ices Curator Emma Logan\, this engaging discussion offers insight into the
  intersection of artmaking\, education\, and community connection.
LOCATION:Petaluma Arts Center
