SUMMARY:Braulio Barrera y Somos El Son
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260712T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260712T160000
UID:2607027BzXXpQ7C0OHb975JA4EKw
DESCRIPTION:Braulio Barrera was born in Lima\, Peru on June 29\, 1969.  A
  singer and composer\, he comes from a family of traditional Peruvian mus
 ic artists.  Braulio began to explore salsa in 2002 in Los Angeles\, Cali
 fornia.  He recorded a soundtrack for the film Diarios de un motociclista
 \, directed by Gustavo Santoalaya\, which won the Golden Globe Awards.\n
 \nHe moved to San Francisco in 2011 and there he sang with the Pacific Ma
 mbo orchestra with which he won a Grammy for best Latin album\, in the sa
 me category with Carlos Vives and Marc Antony.  In 2013 Braulio created 
 his orchestra called Somos el son\, with which he had great success due t
 o the energy and musical quality\, playing in San Francisco Clubs\, many 
 salsa festivals and congresses\, and released his first salsa album title
 d Como te soñe\, with original songs composed by himself.  Braulio curr
 ently does shows for children in several public schools through a program
  of the San Francisco Symphony.
LOCATION:Vino Godfather
URL:https://events.vinogodfather.com/braulio-barrera-y-somos-el-son/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
