BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Front Porch Revival - Orchid Killers & JT Trawick with Alex Shar
 ps
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260712T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260712T200000
UID:260626R_zpJa26ekOncz6NfHIPDw
DESCRIPTION:Front Porch Revival: An Evening of Old-School Folk & Cowboy Sw
 ing\n\nStep into an evening of authentic\, foot-stomping roots music as th
 e Front Porch Revival comes to Santa Rosa. This special performance brings
  together raw storytelling\, vintage acoustic tones\, and incredible music
 ianship for a night that bridges the gap between yesterday and today.\n\nT
 he Lineup:\n\nThe Orchid Killers: Local Sonoma County favorites and mainst
 ays of the Northbay Hootenanny scene\, this dynamic outfit is fronted by K
 aren Frindell Teuscher \\(banjo\, vocals\\) and Kevin Teuscher \\(1936 gui
 tar\, vocals\\)\, alongside Brian Carlisle \\(fiddle\\) and Henry Nagle \\
 (guitar\, pedal steel\\).\n\nJT Trawick ft. Alex Sharps: Ozark Original\, 
 JT Trawick delivers a commanding dose of original\, old-school Ozark Mount
 ain folk and Cowboy Swing. Joining him on stage is Gold Country fiddle phe
 nom Alex Sharps \\(Hot Buttered Rum\, Windy Hill\\)\, whose blazing\, soul
 ful fiddle work breathes vibrant life into every timeless arrangement.\n\n
 What to Expect:\n\n"Banjo runs like rain on a shingle roof\, roadside cree
 ks on a winter drive... and echoes of another time in the harmonies..."\n\
 nExpect a warm\, high-energy matinee filled with rich vocal harmonies\, dr
 iving old-time acoustic jams\, and the haunting ghosts of classic country 
 legends. Whether you love traditional bluegrass\, western swing\, or intim
 ate storytelling\, this lineup promises a captivated room and an unforgett
 able community vibe.\n\nGrab your tickets now for an incredible afternoon 
 of traditional American roots music!
LOCATION:The Lost Church Santa Rosa
URL:https://thelostchurch.my.salesforce-sites.com/ticket#/instances/a0FUh0
 00009bI41MAE
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Stories from the Light: Gears\, Grease\, Guts and Glow
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260712T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260712T153000
UID:260624jxOI6giyvUmzU71foMogUA
DESCRIPTION:Join a park ranger in historic lighthouse keeper attire and st
 ep into the living machinery of the Point Reyes Lighthouse\, where precisi
 on engineering and human dedication work hand in hand. Down in the tower\,
  you’ll encounter the lighthouse’s intricate system of gears\, weights
 \, and bearings\, all designed to turn a massive lens with perfect timing.
  But behind every smooth rotation was a keeper who was listening\; winding
  it through storms\, troubleshooting its quirks\, and safeguarding sailors
  through dangerous waters. The life of a keeper was not for everyone. Disc
 over how this 19th‑century engineering masterpiece and the people who te
 nded it worked together to create an unwavering promise of light for 105 y
 ears. Drop-in anytime between 1:30 PM and 3:30 PM. Programs are approximat
 ely 15 minutes long and occur on a rolling basis. Please note: This progra
 m meets in the large building at the bottom of the Lighthouse stairs. The 
 climb is strenuous and program participants should be prepared to climb ab
 out 25 to 30 stories worth of stairs on the way back up. Bring water\, wea
 r appropriate footwear and make sure to bring layers\, as weather at the P
 oint Reyes Lighthouse can change quickly
LOCATION:Point Reyes National Seashore
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/1356647506307343/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
