BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:No Cell Sundays: Marcus & Devin
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260712T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260712T143000
UID:2606081gYPXOZAi0G5UiX-1qbfCw
DESCRIPTION:**Unplug and Groove: P-Butta Live at the Vineyard**\n\nJoin us
  for No Cell Sundays with P-Butta\, a local powerhouse trio that's been ma
 king Sonoma County move for decades.\n\nP-Butta is the instrumental side p
 roject of the musicians from Rising Tide\, the original Groundation band. 
 With Marcus Urani on keyboards\, Ryan Newman on bass\, and Paul Spina on d
 rums\, this three-piece brings together four decades of funk\, soul\, and 
 jazz mastery that satisfies any musical palate.\n\nExpect to hear groovy c
 overs from legendary artists like The Meters\, Booker T & the M.G.'s\, Her
 bie Hancock\, Donnie Hathaway\, Cannonball Adderley\, and even the Beastie
  Boys. Whether you're a jazz head or just love good vibes\, P-Butta delive
 rs the perfect soundtrack for a Sunday afternoon in wine country.\n\n**Wha
 t's No Cell Sundays?**\n\nIt's simple: disconnect from your devices\, reco
 nnect with great wine\, live music\, and the people around you. *Check yo
 ur phone with us at the door and receive a complimentary tasting.* Bring 
 a blanket\, grab a glass\, and spend your Sunday the way it was meant to b
 e spent.
LOCATION:Hook & Ladder Winery
URL:https://www.hookandladderwinery.com/event/no-cell-sundays-p-butta
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sundays in the Plaza: Laura Benitez and the Heartache (Country / A
 mericana)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260712T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260712T150000
UID:260606bQKjT2jCm0uULKUnWN22vA
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a series of relaxing afternoons in the plaza this 
 summer from 1:00 PM - 3:00 PM. Each week will feature a live music perform
 ance from a local band or performer. Not to be confused with Tuesdays in t
 he Plaza\, this is a great opportunity to bring a picnic\, sit back\, rela
 x and enjoy the melodies.\n\nAbout the music: Storyteller\, content creato
 r\, songwriter and all around creative force\, Laura Benitez has been maki
 ng her mark on stage and screen for more than two decades. Specializing in
  classic country music\, she recently wrote the theme song for the Dingus 
 of the Week podcast created by popular author and activist Lyz Lenz\, and 
 her song "Our Remember Whens" received an honorable mention in the America
 n Songwriter lyric contest in January of 2016. Taking her musical cues fro
 m the heavily rock influenced Bakersfield sound\, and her lyric inspiratio
 n from her favorite songwriters Dolly Parton and Loretta Lynn\, Laura bega
 n writing songs in 2008.
LOCATION:Healdsburg Plaza
URL:https://healdsburg.gov/899/Sundays-in-the-Plaza
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
