DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260712T183000
UID:2605129097tIVLLk2aAfev3w4wgg
DESCRIPTION:This summer\, Valley Players invites you to six unforgettable 
 evenings of theatre — featuring staged readings of bold\, original works
  by both veteran playwrights and emerging talents. Be the first to experie
 nce these sparkling new works brought to life!\n\n**June 14:** *Mother\, I
  Could Kill You* by Barbara A. Silverstone\n\n**June 28:** A Night of One-
 Acts\n\n*When We Ceased to Be?* by Jack Bushnell\n\n*At Midspan on the And
 y Warhol* by Kirk Johnson\n\n**July 12:** *Waldorf School* by Nate Currier
 \n\n**July 26:** *Deadly Pursuits* by Lorraine Midanik\n\n**August 9:** A 
 Night of Shorts\n\n*Madam Director* by Gary A. Davis\n\n*Date Night* by Ba
 rbara A. Silverstone\n\n*Table in the Air* by Rex McGregor\n\n*An Empowere
 d Woman* by Barbara Anderson\n\n**August 23:** *Night Shift* by Mack Wrigh
 t\n\nEach play will be followed by a short talk-back.\n\nBuy tickets onlin
 e and save $3 off the at the door price! Tickets can be pre-purchased onli
 ne or by calling 707-948-6273 for $12 or purchased at the door beginning 3
 0 minutes before showtime for $15.
LOCATION:NVEF Discovery Campus
URL:https://www.valley-players.com/2026/03/06/valley-players-summer-2026-s
 taged-reading-series/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sonoma Sundays on the Plaza - Heidi Evelyn & the Savoy Sweethearts
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260712T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260712T170000
UID:260502urZHfsk-3kOqsn4PmCkdYg
DESCRIPTION:This summer\, Music in Place and the City of Sonoma invite you
  to soak up the sunshine\, sip local wine\, and dance to live music at the
  Sonoma Plaza Grinstead Amphitheater during Sonoma Sundays On the Plaza\, 
 a free concert series running June 7 through October 4\, 2026.\n\nThis wee
 k's lineup features Heidi Evelyn and the Savoy Sweethearts! If you love to
  swing out to hot riffs or swoon to sweet melodies\, the Savoy Sweethearts
  are the band for you. They uniquely capture the sound of the late 1930s a
 nd early 1940s\, at the birth of the swing era and the lindy hop craze. Th
 e band features a roster of jazz masters with a passion for historical aut
 henticity\, powered by a true sense of rhythm and drive. The band features
  a blend of vintage arrangements and spontaneous creativity.\n\nSonoma Sun
 days are free and open to all\, thanks to the generous support of the Sono
 ma Community Center\, The Dawn Redwoods Trust\, and the McNeely Family Fou
 ndation.\n\nPack your picnic\, bring your dancing shoes\, and meet us on t
 he Plaza!
LOCATION:Grinstead Amphitheater
URL:https://musicinplace.org/event/sonoma-sundays-on-the-plaza-7-12/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sunday Funday at Sonoma Botanical Garden
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260712T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260712T160000
UID:260412o70QOiMSEUyWqm5c_lLtiw
DESCRIPTION:Art Escape is rolling over to Sonoma Botanical Garden with Art
  Van Gogh\, our mobile art studio!\n\nJoin us for crafts and creative fun 
 for all ages. Our wonderful teachers\, Susan & Cristina\, will guide you i
 n creating Flores Gigantes \\(Giant Garden Flowers\\).\n\nParticipants wil
 l color pre-cut cardstock petal templates using bright paint sticks inspir
 ed by Oaxacan color traditions—yellows\, pinks\, reds\, oranges\, and bl
 ues. They’ll layer and assemble the petals into oversized flowers. Young
 er children can keep it simple with bold color\, while older participants 
 can add patterns\, dots\, and linework inspired by alebrije-style detailin
 g.\n\nRSVP to us at info@artescapesonoma.com to join for FREE!
LOCATION:Sonoma Botanical Garden
URL:https://artescapesonoma.jumbula.com/Summer2026/ArtVanGoghSundayFundaya
 tSonomaBotanicalGardensJuly
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
