BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jumpstart Your Art
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260713T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260713T160000
UID:260629yLw3jvzeY0uUV43I_GFfGA
DESCRIPTION:Every person experiences an ebb and flow to the tides of their
  creativity. We will share space together to design\, exchange ideas\, and
  hold ourselves accountable to our unique interests! The first portion of 
 our time together will involve a check-in discussion of ‘what is'\, lead
 ing into ‘what could be'. The talk will be facilitated by Erin Partridge
 \, an art therapist with a long history of supporting people in reengaging
  with creativity. After our initial talk\, we will have some time to indiv
 idually focus on our creative practices in the space of the gallery. Befor
 e we close\, we will share anything that came up in the process. Bring you
 r ideas\, a project\, and an interest in creative community. Please be min
 dful of what you choose to show up with-something quiet\, easy to clean up
 \, and non-disruptive to your fellow creatives. Not sure where to begin? S
 ome basic materials are available\, thanks to a donation from  Blick Art M
 aterials . Open for all ages-youth under 12 with an adult chaperone please
 ! Mondays\, 1-4 PM Facilitator: Erin Partridge
URL:https://creativesonoma.org/event/jumpstart-your-art/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Roots of the Valleys: A Photography Exhibit
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260713T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260713T170000
UID:260708StnIPjIHMUK3KK1zK2HUAA
DESCRIPTION:**The San Geronimo Valley Community Center proudly presents: R
 oots of the Valleys Photography Exhibition in the Maurice Del Mue Gallerie
 s from July 7 - 31.  There will be a reception for the artists on July 12
 \, from 4 - 7 pm.** \n\n **Roots of the Valleys** brings together the wor
 k of 20 local professional and amateur photographers in a collective explo
 ration of the San Geronimo and Nicasio Valleys. Through images of landscap
 e\, people\, wildlife\, architecture\, and everyday life\, the exhibition 
 reflects the distinctive character\, history\, and sense of place that def
 ine these rural communities. Together\, these diverse perspectives create 
 a visual portrait of the valleys and the connections that root us to them.
 \n\n Artists Include:\n\nGisela Alvarado\, John Andrew Murphy\, Velvy App
 leton\, Marian Cremin\, Cindy Davis\, Donn DeAngelo\, Jerry Draper\, Julie
  Egger\, Martha Elizabeth Ture\, Roberta Floden\, Harlan Floyd\, Sr.\, Dav
 id Glaubinger\, Sasha Gulish\, Amena Hajjar\, Mia Johnson-Martinez\, Sarah
  Killingsworth\, Richard Lang\, David Lee Hoffman\, Avis Licht\, Priscilla
  Patey\, Laura Persson\, Todd Pickering\, Taylor Rechtschaffen\, Juliette 
 Valente
LOCATION:San Geronimo Valley Community Center
URL:https://sangeronimovalleycommunitycenter.eventcalendarapp.com/roots-of
 -the-valleys-photography-exhibit
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
