BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Children's Wonderland Storytime
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260715T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260715T114500
UID:260707-3oSp38DXEiQIVdTbTc98A
DESCRIPTION:Join us at Children's Wonderland Park for fun\, songs\, and st
 ories every Wednesday at 11:15am! This weekly storytime runs from May 13-O
 ctober 28 thanks to a partnership with GVRD. Location: 360 Glenn St. Valle
 jo\, CA 94590 Free parking in the lot between Children's Wonderland and Va
 llejo Parent Nursery School. Enter through the castle doors guarded by cro
 codiles to the magical world of Children's Wonderland! Climbing features i
 nclude a pirate ship\, train\, "steaming" teapot and much more! Admission:
  Admission to Children's Wonderland is free for Vallejo residents. Visitor
 s from outside of Vallejo may be asked to pay an entrance fee per person. 
 Children must be accompanied by an adult\, and adults may not enter withou
 t a child. Weather: Dress appropriately! The storytelling area has covered
  seating\, and it can be chilly in the mornings during the spring and fall
 . It warms up quickly during the summer. Children's Wonderland will remain
  closed on rainy days. To check for closures\, please visithttps://www.gvr
 d.org/children-s-wonderland. In case of unexpected park closures\, familie
 s are invited to spend the day playing at the Vallejo Springstowne Library
 .
LOCATION:Vallejo Springstowne Library
URL:https://solanolibrary.libnet.info/event/16325899
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Santa Rosa Wednesday Night Market
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260715T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260715T000000
UID:260526FnAs1mNZyU-5LDZe1Kp9bg
DESCRIPTION:The Santa Rosa Wednesday Night Market is a beloved free commun
 ity event that's been a tradition for 37 years and brings people together 
 to celebrate local culture\, small businesses\, and the vibrant spirit of 
 downtown. Our mission is to create an inclusive\, welcoming public space w
 here residents and visitors can gather to enjoy great food\, live entertai
 nment\, and unique local vendors while supporting the economic and social 
 health of our city. This lively open-air street fair features a curated se
 lection of local artisans\, farmers\, food vendors\, and community organiz
 ations. Guests can enjoy live music and performances\, explore handmade go
 ods\, discover fresh local products\, and connect with the people who make
  Sonoma County special. Families are especially welcome. The Market includ
 es a dedicated Kids Zone with free activities for children\, interactive e
 xperiences\, and opportunities for learning and play. Local nonprofit orga
 nizations also participate each week\, sharing information about their pro
 grams and helping strengthen connections across the community. The Wednesd
 ay Night Market is more than an event-it's a celebration of community\, cr
 eativity\, and the local businesses and organizations that help Santa Rosa
  thrive.
LOCATION:Old Courthouse Square
URL:https://www.visitsantarosa.com/events/#jlupcoming-events
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
