BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Thai Cooking Class Benefiting Sonoma Family Meal
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260716T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260716T193000
UID:2607094kuzBiRwUkiiIaNnxT2RZw
DESCRIPTION:Thai Cooking Class with Chef Kanyaa & Tina - July 16\n\n$125.0
 0\n\nJoin Sonoma Family Meal's very own Chef Kanyaa and recent culinary tr
 aining graduate Tina for a unique Thai cooking class featuring favorites f
 rom their homeland. Kanyaa brings her culinary experience and heritage fro
 m the Northeastern Thai region of Isaan\, which is specifically known for 
 it's delectable cuisine and Tina\, also a Thai-born cook\, brings her pass
 ion for food systems and her newfound skills and confidence from the CJT p
 rogram to share with you all.\n\nIn this hands-on two hour class\, you wil
 l learn the breakdown of how to make several traditional Thai specialties 
 and receive the recipes and cooking instructions to take home. You will wo
 rk in teams to prepare all the food under Chef's guidance\, and then enjoy
  the meal together family style at the end!\n\nWHEN: Thursday July 16\, 5-
 7:30pm WHERE: SFM community kitchen\, 1370A Redwood Way\, Petaluma\n\nPLEA
 SE WEAR CLOSE TOED SHOES TO ALL CLASSES\n\nTHE MENU:\n\nVegetable Fresh Sp
 ring Rolls\n\nChicken Khao Soi \\(Northern Thai Curry Noodle Soup\\)\n\nVe
 getable Pad Thai with Tofu\n\nMango Ube Sticky Rice\n\nIf you have a speci
 fic food allergy or have any questions about the menu\, please contact han
 nah@sonomafamilymeal.org.\n\nHear it from our customers:\n\n"Kudos to Chef
  Kanyaa!  We loved the Thai Chicken Curry last night. Cooked perfectly\,
  it was delicious! The egg rolls and dipping sauce so yummy\, I could eat
  those every night." - Karyl\n\nAbout Tina:\n\nYaowalak “Tina” is a Th
 ai-born cook and former nonprofit professional who studied food systems an
 d worked in environmental and community-focused organizations in Thailand.
  Now\, drawing on her family’s market cooking roots and her passion for 
 food\, is building the skills and confidence through Sonoma Family Meal’
 s culinary training program to launch her own business in private cheffing
  and cooking education.\n\nAbout Kanyaa:\n\nOriginally from the Isan regio
 n of Thailand\, Kanyaa is a passionate cook with experience in pastry and 
 much more. She lives in Rohnert Park with her teen son\, and in her free t
 ime\, enjoys preparing the dishes of her homeland\, like chicken over rice
  and noodle soup. As the kitchen assistant\, Kanyaa assists with the kitch
 en’s day-to-day operations\, her favorite part of the role is "cooking f
 or the community."\n\nQuan
LOCATION:Sonoma Family Meal
URL:https://www.sonomafamilymeal.org/store-2/thaicooking
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
