DESCRIPTION:Join us for the 14th annual Northern California yarn lovers ex
 perience from July 17-19\, 2026!\n\nThe Wine Country Yarn Hop consists of 
 5 shops located in the beautiful Wine Country between Petaluma & Ukiah.\n\
 nThe 2026 Yarn Hop is FREE and begins July 17\, 2026 at 10:00am. The Hop i
 s 3 days long\, you can choose to do all 5 shops in one day\, or spread it
  out and hop all weekend.\n\nAll 5 shops are open from 10:00 - 5:00 each d
 ay of the Hop: July 17\, 18 & 19.\n\nYou will receive a passport to be sta
 mped at each shop\, as well as 1 raffle ticket per stop. Participants will
  be entered to win a prize basket at each shop\, AND the Grand Prize baske
 t when a complete passport is turned in. FREE patterns\, and free enamel p
 ins w/ tote or lanyard purchase.\n\nNo need to register - just start hoppi
 ng at any of the 5 shops!\n\nLearn more: winecountryyarnhop.com\n\nPartici
 pating Shops:\n\nFiber Circle Studios- Petaluma\n\nNoma Knits- Sonoma \n\
 nCast Away Yarn Shop- Santa Rosa\n\nPurls of Joy- Healdsburg\n\nPurple Nee
 dle- Ukiah
LOCATION:Cast Away Yarn Shop
URL:https://winecountryyarnhop.com/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:JAD Experience presents LUNAE
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260717T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260717T220000
UID:2607096xXuo7QoIUqLqY_y64DFIA
DESCRIPTION:**JAD Experience**\, the trailblazing series uniting regenerat
 ive cuisine and world-class ballet\, announces **LUNAE**\, its milestone 1
 3th season. Taking place July 17–19 and July 24–26\, LUNAE is an immer
 sive evening of farm-to-table dining\, world-class ballet under the stars\
 , and deep connection with nature.\n\nInspired by the 13 lunar cycles of t
 he year\, LUNAE’s choreography evokes the timeless rhythms of creation\,
  surrender\, and renewal through themes of feminine energy\, light\, and s
 hadow.\n\nPerched atop Tara Firma Farms (3796 I Street Ext.\, Petaluma\, C
 A 94952) with sweeping pastoral views\, LLUNAE delivers on the original so
 cial ritual: shared culinary experience at long tables. Following dinner\,
  an intimate ballet performance unfolds beneath the night sky for just 100
  guests each evening.\n\nEvenings begin with arrival and cocktails from 5:
 30 to 7 p.m.\, followed by dinner from 7 to 8:30 p.m. The experience conti
 nues with the ballet performance from 8:45 to 9:30 p.m.\, and the evening 
 concludes at 10 p.m.\n\nFree parking is available\, and all seating offers
  excellent views of the open-air stage. Because evenings in Petaluma can c
 ool quickly\, guests are encouraged to bring warm layers\; blankets and ho
 t chocolate will also be provided. Guests needing assistance may choose be
 tween a hayride or a shuttle for accessibility.\n\nRenowned choreographer 
 Julia Adam\, an Ottawa native and former San Francisco Ballet principal da
 ncer (1988–2002)\, has created more than 100 works for companies includi
 ng Houston Ballet and the National Ballet of Canada.\n\nFeatured dancers i
 nclude David O’matz (Pittsburgh Ballet Theatre)\, Augi Lehner\, Ryan Wil
 liams\, Saela Rivera-Martinez\, Zoe Lucich (Bay Area\, Houston Ballet)\, H
 arry Warshaw (Ballet Memphis)\, Lily Mangiaruga (New Orleans Ballet Theatr
 e)\, Kelsey Mcfalls (freelance\, Bay Area)\, and Tessa Barbour (Smuin Ball
 et\, Bay Area).\n\nDinner is led by chefs Brian Leitner and Annette Yang o
 f Pearl\, presenting a multi-course menu rooted in the farm and its surrou
 nding network. The evening features dishes such as beef tartare\, summer s
 uccotash\, grilled strip loin\, and seasonal desserts\, alongside substant
 ial vegetarian and vegan offerings.\n\nIngredients are sourced transparent
 ly from Tara Firma Farms and regional partners\, including Umbel Roots\, F
 eed Sonoma\, True Grass Farms\, and Holistic Ag. Beverage pairings include
  wines from Enkidu and Shokrian\, beers from HenHouse and Moonlight Brewin
 g\, and house-made nonalcoholic options.\n\nTara Firma Farms\, a working c
 attle ranch stewarded by JAD co-founder Aaron Lucich\, powers this chef-fa
 rmer artistry.\n\nIn an era shaped by screen addiction and fleeting digita
 l distractions\, LUNAE offers a return to genuine human connection through
  live performance\, communal dining\, and an extraordinary natural setting
 .\n\n“LUNAE follows thirteen lunar cycles\, with each phase shaping the 
 timing and movement of the choreography\,” said **Julia Adam\, Co-Founde
 r & Choreographer**. “The work draws on feminine energy\, expressed thro
 ugh exquisite motion\, repetition\, and release.” \n\n“We need to bec
 ome conscious that we are just a part of the natural system\,” said **Aa
 ron Lucich\, Co-Founder & Tara Firma Farms Managing Partner.** “Land and
  people heal together. LUNAE's farm-driven feasts at long communal tables\
 , grown from our regenerative soils\, model this: dining as unity\, ballet
  as connection\, all under the moon to remind us we're a part of nature's 
 own cycles.”
LOCATION:Tara Firma Farms
URL:https://jadexperience.org/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Roots of the Valleys: A Photography Exhibit
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260717T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260717T170000
UID:260708dsEZNHKVmEOuAI9Vm0x4Lg
DESCRIPTION:**The San Geronimo Valley Community Center proudly presents: R
 oots of the Valleys Photography Exhibition in the Maurice Del Mue Gallerie
 s from July 7 - 31.  There will be a reception for the artists on July 12
 \, from 4 - 7 pm.** \n\n **Roots of the Valleys** brings together the wor
 k of 20 local professional and amateur photographers in a collective explo
 ration of the San Geronimo and Nicasio Valleys. Through images of landscap
 e\, people\, wildlife\, architecture\, and everyday life\, the exhibition 
 reflects the distinctive character\, history\, and sense of place that def
 ine these rural communities. Together\, these diverse perspectives create 
 a visual portrait of the valleys and the connections that root us to them.
 \n\n Artists Include:\n\nGisela Alvarado\, John Andrew Murphy\, Velvy App
 leton\, Marian Cremin\, Cindy Davis\, Donn DeAngelo\, Jerry Draper\, Julie
  Egger\, Martha Elizabeth Ture\, Roberta Floden\, Harlan Floyd\, Sr.\, Dav
 id Glaubinger\, Sasha Gulish\, Amena Hajjar\, Mia Johnson-Martinez\, Sarah
  Killingsworth\, Richard Lang\, David Lee Hoffman\, Avis Licht\, Priscilla
  Patey\, Laura Persson\, Todd Pickering\, Taylor Rechtschaffen\, Juliette 
 Valente
LOCATION:San Geronimo Valley Community Center
URL:https://sangeronimovalleycommunitycenter.eventcalendarapp.com/roots-of
 -the-valleys-photography-exhibit
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Back pOrchEstra at River Front Cafe. Fridays On The Deck  July 17.
  5:30-8
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260717T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260717T200000
UID:260708dCwbBBQLwkKIlF4-Uty76Q
DESCRIPTION:Back pOrchEstra!...OUTDOOR show at River Front Cafe. "Fridays 
 On The Deck\,"" July 17\, Fri. Eve.\, 5:30-8:00\n\n224 B Street Petaluma\,
  CA 94952\n\n\\(707\\) 347-5147\n\n...Candy Girard\, Gary Potterton\, Tim 
 Eschliman\, Luis Rodriguez and Jen Rund... We'll be performing Original an
 d vintage Roots Rock\, Americana\, Country Blues\, Singer/Songwriter and W
 estern Swing with rich acoustic tones...\n\nWe have a single out!: https:/
 /orcd.co/lxz1l6v "I'm Wild About My Lovin'"\, celebrating the new "Stories
  In The Heart" album\, listen now!: https://orcd.co/5xga7nr\n\n"...What se
 ts 'Stories In The Heart' apart is its sense of balance. Resonator guitar\
 , violin\, bass\, drums\, percussion\, dobro\, and Telecaster create a fle
 xible\, roots-forward palette that allows Back Porchestra to move between 
 styles fluidly. The songs echo traditions without reenacting them\, keepin
 g one foot in the past and the other firmly planted in the present." - Vin
 ce's Hot Picks \\(Best of 2026\\) New Releases Now\n\n"The guitars slam li
 ke saloon doors\, the violin traces lines that oscillate between melanchol
 y and jubilation\, the rhythm section moves forward with a tranquil groove
  that never rushes but never falters... Back pOrchEstra delivers a luminou
 s\, earthy\, profoundly human record. An album that makes you want to sit 
 on a porch\, watch the sunset\, and let the stories do their work...." - F
 red Delforge\, Zicazine \\(translated from French\\)\n\nOutdoor dining & d
 ancing event! ...on the ever lovelier River Front Petaluma Turing Basin sc
 ene. River Front Cafe sez: "We create our dishes freshly here in our kitch
 en. Local farm vegetables and locally raised beef & chicken\, served with 
 fresh bread from a local bakery. Breakfast& Lunch served daily. Mediterran
 ean/ American dishes"\n\nBack pOrchEstra is a compact Shelter-in-Place-ins
 pired musical combo ....going back to the basics... Formed for the first t
 ime the locked-down summer of 2020. The band draws from new original mater
 ial as well as reworked classics by Hank Williams\, Taj Mahal\, Dan Hicks\
 , Big Bill Broonzy\, Bob Wills\, Bobby Charles ...even Christmas Jug Band 
 tunes\n\n... check out the "Dusty Road I'm On" video: https://youtu.be/jj0
 IIkUyrE4 ...a twangy roots rock number with a Cajun flavor and hints of Je
 sse Ed Davis and Sid Page....\n\nThe previous single\, the Neo-Motown/Levo
 n Helm style "Ever Think About It\," is here: https://orcd.co/qo5579q\n\nL
 Ps\, CDs\, and USB-Music Cards available all over\, including https://www.
 globerecords.com\n\nmore at... https://www.BackpOrchEstra.com\n\nBandCamp:
  https://backporchestra.bandcamp.com\n\nyouTube: https://www.youtube.com/p
 laylist?list=PLOTwG2XEiO2O8c0dEI-7hlpI8nr7apiNf\n\nBluesky: https://bsky.a
 pp/profile/backporchestra.bsky.social\n\nReverb Nation: https://www.reverb
 nation.com/backporchestra\n\nFacebook: https://www.facebook.com/BackPorchE
 stra/\n\nInstagram: https://www.instagram.com/backporchestra/\n\n\\#rootsr
 ock\n\n\\#americanrootsmusic\n\n\\#americanamusic\n\n\\#rockabillymusic\n\
 n\\#twangyguitar\n\n\\#backporchestra\n\n\\#acousticmusic\n\n\\#adultalbum
 alternative\n\n\\#singersongwriter\n\n\\#folkmusic\n\n\\#folkrock
LOCATION:River Front Cafe
URL:https://www.BackpOrchEstra.com/shows.html
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
