BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Redwood Writers General Meeting - Jordan Rosenfeld
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260718T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260718T133000
UID:260709PWC1nHVuuUyV-gYxeQAsuQ
DESCRIPTION:Jordan Rosenfeld: When the Character is You – Curating a Per
 sona in Memoir\n\nPlease bring something savory or sweet to share in our p
 otluck!\n\nThis workshop helps memoirists takes control of the narrative t
 hrough a powerful persona that balance writers’ roles as both narrator t
 elling the story\, a character in the story. Memoirs often deal with diffi
 cult\, personal and intimate material that has to be selectively shaped an
 d revealed. Curating a persona allows you to control and mold your narrati
 ve exactly as you want and still tell your truth. We’ll look at what it 
 means to create a written persona\, to curate a voice that is a stylized\,
  narrative version of you\, and to be intentional with your truth at the s
 entence level.\n\nAbout the Presenter:\n\nJordan Rosenfeld is author of th
 e novels Fallout\, Women in Red\, and Forged in Grace\, and eight books
  on the craft of writing\, including the forthcoming Writing Through the 
 Pause: Mining Midlife for Powerful Writing\, as well as The Sound of Stor
 y: Developing Voice and Tone in Writing\, How to Write a Page-Turner\, th
 e bestselling Make a Scene\, Writing the Intimate Character\, A Writer
 ’s Guide to Persistence\, Writing Deep Scenes \\(with Martha Alderson\
 \)\, and Write Free \\(with Rebecca Lawton\\). Her freelance writing has 
 been published in hundreds of publications\, including: The Atlantic\, The
  New York Times\, Publisher’s Weekly\, Salon\, Scientific American\, The
  Rumpus\, Writer’s Digest Magazine\, The Washington Post and many more. 
 She is also a freelance manuscript editor\, writing coach and teaches onli
 ne classes.
LOCATION:Finley Center
URL:https://redwoodwriters.org/july-2026-jordan-rosenfeld/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
