DESCRIPTION:Explore the musical connections between England and Bohemia th
 rough works by Dvořák\, Vaughan Williams\, and Rebecca Clarke. This rhap
 sodic evening highlights rich folk traditions and lyrical chamber music pa
 ired with wine selections from premier Sonoma vineyards. Arrive early for 
 a free pre-concert lecture led by musicologist Elaine Fitz Gibbon. Concert
  duration: approximately 2 hours with intermission.\n\nThe Valley of the M
 oon Music Festival returns July 11–26\, 2026\, with Postcards from Dvoř
 ák\, a season inspired by the travels\, influences\, and cultural connect
 ions behind the composer’s music. Set in the heart of Sonoma Valley\, th
 e festival brings together internationally acclaimed musicians for histori
 cally informed performances that blend world-class classical music with th
 e beauty and charm of wine country.
