BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Summer Restorative Yoga
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260718T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260718T113000
UID:260427Y4E6_RIWN0aej0wQyzdomA
DESCRIPTION:Begin your summer Saturday mornings with a calming session of 
 restorative yoga at the Garden - an invitation to slow down\, breathe deep
 ly\, and reconnect with yourself in a peaceful natural setting. Whether yo
 u’re looking to unwind from a busy week or manage ongoing stress\, this 
 beginner-friendly class offers a gentle path toward physical and emotional
  balance. Join us to explore the deeply relaxing practices of Yoga Nidra\,
  Yin Yoga\, and restorative postures—all designed to release tension\, c
 alm the nervous system\, and support mindful rest. Classes take place indo
 ors in our Center for Learning & Engagement\, surrounded by the peaceful e
 nergy of the Garden\, it’s the perfect setting to unwind. Sessions are l
 ed by our thoughtful and experienced partners at Sonoma Yoga\, who special
 ize in making yoga both accessible and engaging. These sessions are led by
  our thoughtful and experienced partners at Sonoma Yoga\, a community-cent
 ered studio with over 20 years of experience and a dynamic team of yoga\, 
 fitness\, and meditation guides to support your practice. Please dress acc
 ordingly and bring water.
LOCATION:Sonoma Botanical Garden
URL:https://sonomabg.org/visit/spirit-guides/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sunset Spirit Sound Bath
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260718T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260718T200000
UID:260427H6TIdfsJck-7vo88gWApdg
DESCRIPTION:In celebration of our Spirit Guides exhibition\, join Glen El
 len–based practitioners Amelia Belle and Bob Rudorf for a restorative op
 en air sound bath inspired by the wisdom\, symbolism\, and grounding prese
 nce of the natural world. For over a decade\, Amelia and Bob have used sou
 nd and guided meditation as tools for transformation. In this immersive ex
 perience\, crystal singing bowls and other resonant instruments blend with
  the natural sounds of the Garden\, creating a meditative soundscape that 
 echoes the themes of Spirit Guides—connection\, reflection\, and inner a
 wakening. For this July 18 sound bath\, Amelia and Bob with be joined by r
 enown Ceremonial Sound Practitioner & Healing Performance Artist\, René J
 enkins. For more than 30 years\, René performs sound healing concerts\, b
 lessings and ceremonies for individuals and special groups throughout the 
 US and internationally. While embracing the ancestral wisdom from cross-cu
 ltural anthropologist Angeles Arrien\, Kashaya-Pomo elder/healer Lorin Smi
 th\, and renowned South American sound healer/musician Tito La Rosa\, Ren
 é raises consciousness-vibration through Sacred Sound and Intention. Held
  in the Garden’s outdoor grassy amphitheater at Sonoma Botanical Garden\
 , the session unfolds beneath the open sky as day transitions into evening
 . As you settle into stillness\, you’ll be gently bathed in calming freq
 uencies designed to quiet the mind\, relax the body\, and open the heart. 
 The vibrations of the crystal bowls move through you\, helping to release 
 tension\, restore balance\, and cultivate a deeper sense of presence. Open
  to all levels\, this experience invites you to reconnect with nature and 
 yourself—an opportunity to pause\, reflect\, and attune to the rhythms o
 f the living landscape.
LOCATION:Sonoma Botanical Garden
URL:https://sonomabotanicalgarden.ticketing.veevartapp.com/tickets/view/li
 st/sunset-spirit-sound-bath-700-pm-800-pm_1
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
