BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Summer Collectors Lunch Pairing at Lynmar Estate
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260718T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260718T143000
UID:260626OObIx7IsAUyhaDxtyay-lw
DESCRIPTION:Rooted in the bounty of Quail Hill Vineyard\, Lynmar Estate’
 s Summer Collectors Lunch Pairing invites guests to experience the flavors
  of Sonoma County at their seasonal peak. The elevated four-course menu sh
 owcases ingredients harvested from Lynmar’s organically farmed gardens\,
  orchards\, and olive groves. Each course is individually plated and thoug
 htfully paired with Lynmar’s acclaimed estate-grown Pinot Noirs\, Chardo
 nnays\, and sparkling wines\, creating a journey that is both deeply conne
 cted to Sonoma County and globally inspired. Served in the idyllic setting
  of Quail Hill Vineyard\, the experience is further enhanced by a special 
 tableside visit from Estate Chef David Frakes.\n\nCollectors Lunch Pairing
  Menu Summer 2026:\n\nAdam’s Vineyard Chardonnay\, 2022\n\nWarm Organic 
 Popcorn\n\nWhite Corn-Kasundi Salt\, Estate Extra-Virgin Olive Oil\n\nSusa
 nna’s Vineyard Chardonnay\, 2022\n\nThai Green Curry & Coconut Soup\n\nB
 liss Snap Peas & Heirloom Radish\n\nYoung Vines Pinot Noir\, 2021\n\nHeirl
 oom Potato & Cherry Tomato ‘Croustade’\n\nSmoked Bacon-Grain Mustard D
 ressing\n\nSusanna’s Vineyard Pinot Noir\, 2022\n\nRoasted Syrian Seven-
 Spiced Chicken Breast\n\nIndonesian Corn Fritter\, Summer Vegetable Ragout
 \, Balado Sauce\n\nRosé de Blancs Sparkling\, 2021\n\nChilled Vanilla Bur
 nt Basque Cheesecake\n\nRaspberry-Rose Syrup\, Black Tea & Licorice-Poache
 d Cherries\n\nBrown Butter Nilla Cookie\, Candied Lime\n\nEstate Ingredien
 ts:\n\nBay Laurel\, Cherries\, Chives\, Edible Flowers\, Lemons\, Olive Oi
 l\, Peas\, Potatoes\, Radishes\, Raspberries\, Thyme\, Tomatoes\, Zucchini
  and more!\n\nMenu by Estate Chef David Frakes\n\nReservations are require
 d. Maximum group size is six guests.
LOCATION:Lynmar Estate
URL:https://lynmarestate.com/reservation/type/collectors-lunch-pairing/ 
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Public Garden Tour
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260718T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260718T140000
UID:260605vS_faKJ7xk-_Pd3Pt1Gz8w
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a guided tour of the Occidental Arts & Ecology Cen
 ter's demonstration gardens and living landscapes. Led by rotating OAEC st
 aff\, these tours offer an opportunity to explore our diverse food\, medic
 inal\, pollinator\, and native plant gardens while learning about the ecol
 ogical principles that guide our work. \n\nWhen: Tours start at 1 pm ever
 y first and third Saturday of the month\, April through October. \n\nWher
 e: Tours start and end at the OAEC Nursery. 15290 Coleman Valley Rd\, Occi
 dental\, CA 95465. Upper Driveway. \n\nImportant Information:\n\nNo regis
 tration required—just show up!\n\nPlease use the second driveway and par
 k in the upper lot near the greenhouses.\n\nThe tour route includes steep 
 hills and unpaved dirt and gravel paths. Sturdy shoes\, a brimmed hat\, an
 d weather-appropriate layers are recommended.\n\nIf you require mobility s
 upport or have other accessibility needs\, please call ahead so we can acc
 ommodate you. Monday–Friday\, contact the main office at \\(707\\) 874-1
 557 ext. 101.\n\nA highlight of every tour is the OAEC Nursery\, a nonprof
 it nursery dedicated to uplifting ecologically and culturally important pl
 ants. The nursery features a wide selection of perennial food crops\, medi
 cinal and native plants\, and an ever-evolving collection of annual vegeta
 bles and herbs adapted to our region.
LOCATION:Occidental Arts and Ecology Center
URL:https://oaec.org/events/tours/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Seaweed Foraging on the Sonoma Coast
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260718T074500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260718T103000
UID:260528z2crhuKT5kik5EkLo_gICQ
DESCRIPTION:This 2.5 hour guided morning foray will meet on the Sonoma Coa
 st\, and be followed by a talk on what you collected\, the ecology of seaw
 eed\, and how to cook your harvest. You can expect to collect up to 10 lbs
 . of raw edible seaweed. This is a coastal forage during low tide. You won
 't need to get in the ocean\, but we recommend wearing rain boots. Please 
 note this event is for ages 9 and up. An educational hands-on workshop · 
  Learn a new food skill ·  Explore the normally-underwater inter tidal 
 zone at a negative low tide ·  Connect with your local food system ·  
 Enjoy nutritional-rich umami direct from the source.
LOCATION:Bodega Bay\, CA
URL:https://www.foragesf.com/seaweed-foraging-sonoma
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
