SUMMARY:Introduction to Birds & Their Physiology
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260719T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260719T110000
UID:260625o_g6D2zOzEKXL--Hng4d5g
DESCRIPTION:Join Sugarloaf volunteer Steve Callow on this introduct
 ion to bird ID with an emphasis on their physiology. The outing
  begins at the main parking area and heads out Creekside Nature
  Trail and uphill to Hillside Trail. The group will have the o
 ption to complete the Hillside-Meadow loop or go as far as they
 'd like and backtrack to the main lot.\n\nTickets are $10 for g
 eneral audiences\, $5 for students\, youth (12-17 year olds must
  be accompanied by a parent or legal guardian)\, Sugarloaf  mem
 bers\, Sugarloaf or RFO volunteers\, and free for children 8-11.
  Not recommended for children younger than 8. **Tickets day-of o
 n site are $15 and might not be available.** Wear comfortable c
 lothing\, appropriate footwear for rocky/slippery trails\, and sun
  protection. Bring at least a quart of water\, binoculars/birding
  guides (if you have them)\, and if you desire\, a snack. Park
 ing fees apply.
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/birdphysiology26
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Stories from the Light: Gears\, Grease\, Guts and Glow
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260719T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260719T153000
UID:2606241sAITso0TEW6njMVKK21Cw
DESCRIPTION:Join a park ranger in historic lighthouse keeper attire and st
 ep into the living machinery of the Point Reyes Lighthouse\, where precisi
 on engineering and human dedication work hand in hand. Down in the tower\,
  you’ll encounter the lighthouse’s intricate system of gears\, weights
 \, and bearings\, all designed to turn a massive lens with perfect timing.
  But behind every smooth rotation was a keeper who was listening\; winding
  it through storms\, troubleshooting its quirks\, and safeguarding sailors
  through dangerous waters. The life of a keeper was not for everyone. Disc
 over how this 19th‑century engineering masterpiece and the people who te
 nded it worked together to create an unwavering promise of light for 105 y
 ears. Drop-in anytime between 1:30 PM and 3:30 PM. Programs are approximat
 ely 15 minutes long and occur on a rolling basis. Please note: This progra
 m meets in the large building at the bottom of the Lighthouse stairs. The 
 climb is strenuous and program participants should be prepared to climb ab
 out 25 to 30 stories worth of stairs on the way back up. Bring water\, wea
 r appropriate footwear and make sure to bring layers\, as weather at the P
 oint Reyes Lighthouse can change quickly
LOCATION:Point Reyes National Seashore
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/1356647506307343/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Historic Trees at Jack London State Historic Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260719T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260719T113000
UID:260622BHNh2JdgKkKBjxwG_YkdrQ
DESCRIPTION:Join a 2.5-mile guided walk along historic trails through Beau
 ty Ranch and down to the Wolf House ruins to explore the trees that helped
  shape Jack London’s property and vision for the land. Along the way\, l
 earn about London’s ambitious eucalyptus planting project\, heritage orc
 hard trees\, and other notable specimens that have been part of the ranch
 ’s landscape for generations.\n\nFrom the cottage gardens and Jack’s b
 eloved coast live oak to the remnants of the Wolf House orchard\, this lei
 surely walk reveals the rich natural and cultural history of Beauty Ranch 
 through its most iconic trees. Discover how these living landmarks reflect
  London’s agricultural experimentation\, landscape design\, and lasting 
 influence on the land.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/events/historic-trees-of-beauty-ranch-2026/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
