BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Gathering in Peace
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260719T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260719T150000
UID:260616wl3hwqUJsUCcyPKwJjf6Dw
DESCRIPTION:with Zenju Earthlyn Manuel Osho and Rev. Shinmu Tamori Gibson\
 n\nWe are navigating a world that can often appear fractured with greed\, 
 hate\, and delusion which calls on us to hold space for both personal and 
 collective peace. Often\, we might feel adrift and isolated by systemic ca
 uses and conditions that result in suffering. Buddhist teachings recognize
  that our liberation is inextricably bound to the liberation of all beings
 . If we are to achieve collective freedom\, we must engage in practices op
 enly and include all beings in our circle of love\, peace and justice. Our
  efforts can become a part of our daily practice to create individual and 
 collective sanctuaries.\n\nIn this daylong\, we will engage in chanting\, 
 meditation\, ritual and ceremony to invoke collective peace in the world. 
 We will discuss the relevant teachings of Buddha for our times and turn ou
 r focus on the wisdom we have honed.
LOCATION:Spirit Rock Meditation Center
URL:https://spirit-rock.secure.retreat.guru/program/gathering-in-peace-zm1
 d26/?lang=en
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Exhibit: Local Color
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260719T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260719T180000
UID:260616jaN9pK53Dk-pvmDf-X4Bug
DESCRIPTION:Date: FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE  6/15/26\n\n**JULY EXHIBIT: LOC
 AL COLOR**\n\nEXHIBIT DATES:  **June 29 – July 26\, 2026**\n\n**RECEPT
 ION: SATURDAY\, July 4\, 2026\, 3-6 pm: Join us to meet Linda Barretta  
 and Gallery artists\;  Learn about their art and celebrate the show.  
 Be sure to take part in the Gallery’s free monthlong drawing for a beaut
 iful work by a Gallery artist.  Refreshments will be served.**\n\nSonoma
  County artist\, **Linda Barretta** presents **Local Color\,** a collecti
 on unveiling new oil paintings that tap into the vivid natural hues found 
 in our region’s breathtaking beauty.  From flowers to vineyards\, colo
 r takes a starring role in these works.  The deep purple hills in “Sun
 flower Daze” intensify the golden sweep of the sunflowers.  A peach tr
 ee celebrates the season with a glorious pink floral display in “Spring 
 Blooms.”  In “Winery Farm and Gardens\,” framed through a natural 
 arch of trees\, a sunlit vineyard draws the viewer.  “We are so fortun
 ate to live in Sonoma wine country – it’s stunning beauty is a daily i
 nspiration to pick up my brushes and paint\,” commented Barretta. \n\nL
 iving in Healdsburg\, Sonoma wine country is Barretta’s homebase.  She
  developed her impressionist style and skills through numerous hours of pl
 ein air painting and studying with master artists.  When Barretta create
 s the composition\, she is observing the play of light and colors that wil
 l highlight the compelling quality of the scene.  Her aim is to translat
 e her inspiration to the viewer.  From the rough sketch to the final bru
 shstroke\, this is the task she loves.  Barretta participates in the Art
  Trails Open Studio program and her works are exhibited regionally and thr
 oughout the country\,\n\nMeet the artist: Barretta will host the Gallery o
 n July 4\, 6 & 26\, 2:30 – 6pm and July 22\, 11am to 2:30 pm.\n\nThe Sta
 irway Smallworks Showcase features **Beverly Bird’s Birds by Bird\,** a
  collection of acrylic paintings that depict our feathered friends\, big a
 nd small\, in natural habitats.  Rendered in an impressionistic textured
  style\, these works imbue their subjects with a lively spirit.  Bald ea
 gles leave the viewer awed with their regal presence.  While the Steller
  and Scrub jays jauntily hint at their quirky character. In “Circling th
 e Light” the viewer joins a flock of geese on its migratory path. “Bir
 ds enliven our daily existence and their wild spirit provides endless subj
 ect matter\,” Bird noted of her inspiration for the series.\n\nMeet the 
 artist: Bird will host the Gallery on July 22 & 27\, 2:30 – 6pm and July
  29\, 11am to 6 pm.\n\nAlso join us for **ART NITE HEALDSBURG**\, Thursday
 \, July 2\, 5 – 7 pm.  ART NITE Healdsburg\, held the 1st Thursday of
  Every Month\, is a community event celebrating art and creativity with ov
 er 20 galleries participating.  ArtNiteHealdsburg.com.\n\nUpstairs Art G
 allery\, 306 Center Street\, Healdsburg\, CA 95448. (707) 431-4214.: OPEN 
 DAILY: 11am – 6 pm.    **www.upstairsart gallery.net** \n\nFor furt
 her information: Contact: Beverly Bird\, Press Contact\, at bvdrio@sonic.
 net or 707-799-1490.
LOCATION:Upstairs Art Gallery
URL:http://www.upstairsartgallery.net
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Laurie Lewis and Bluegrass Holiday
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260719T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260719T180000
UID:260615TklxmLmIiEaAFlI-8Nzdkw
DESCRIPTION:Grammy-award winning songwriter and bluegrass icon Laurie Lewi
 s brings her band of music-makers once again to UU Petaluma\, re-creating 
 that cozy feeling from the days when she regularly played at the Roaring D
 onkey on Kentucky Street. You can expect to feel that you are in the prese
 nce of beauty\, accomplishment\, and something truly special. \n\nProvidi
 ng an opening set will be Sonoma County's own Bluegrass Holiday. Bluegrass
  Holiday is a top bluegrass band based in the North Bay area of Marin and 
 Sonoma Counties. They entertain audiences with traditional bluegrass that 
 will have them out of their seats dancing one minute and crying in their b
 eer the next. The Bluegrass Holiday musicians bring that crisp 3-part harm
 ony that marks the bluegrass vocal style as well as flashy\, hotshot instr
 umentals. Formed in 2023\, they've played the Cline Country Bluegrass Fest
 ival\, Good Old Fashioned Bluegrass Festival\, San Francisco Bluegrass and
  Old Time Festival\, and the Vern's Stage and the Father's Day Festival of
  the California Bluegrass Association. They can be found entertaining audi
 ences throughout the Bay Area and beyond.\n\nDoors open at 3:30. $25 sugge
 sted donation. Entry at the door only--no advance ticket sales. So come ea
 rly to be sure you snag a seat!All proceeds from the concert go to the art
 ists\, and additional funds raised through refreshments and free-will dona
 tions will support the Sonoma County Sanctuary Coalition\, working to defe
 nd our migrant neighbors as they face increasing threats in the current po
 litical atmosphere.
LOCATION:Unitarian Universalists of Petaluma
URL:https://facebook.com/events/s/sanctuary-concerts-at-uu-petal/196971613
 0576698/?
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
