BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:La Fête Zazou: A Cabaret Jazz and French Culinary Celebration
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260719T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260719T180000
UID:2606034SgsKh9y00CwhGm8JwfBIg
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an unforgettable afternoon and early evening of mu
 sic and French cuisine in honor of Bastille Day\, and our friendship with 
 the people of France\, French immigrants\, and their descendants on Sunday
 \, July 19\, 2026. The Ranch at Sonoma Mountain and Bodega Bay Oyster Comp
 any invite the community to enjoy a French cabaret jazz concert while savo
 ring French appetizers\, oysters\, a four-course meal\, and French wines.\
 n\nSeating will be outside in an intimate setting at Bodega Bay Oyster Com
 pany where guests will enjoy a seasonal French menu highlighting ingredien
 ts from the Ranch at Sonoma Mountain\, oysters from Bodega Bay Oyster Comp
 any\, and carefully selected products from local artisans. Attendees will 
 be transported to the 1920-1940s cabaret jazz scene in Paris with singer L
 aurent Fourgo performing his sweet jazzy sound and some added juke box fav
 orites\; special guest vocalist Isabelle Fontaine will captivate with her 
 rich melodies in a soulful Gypsy style. The band includes power house inst
 rumentalists Jeff Sanford on horns\, Simon Planting on bass\, Karen Kusano
 vich on percussion\, and Jeff Magidson on guitar.  \n\nGuests are encoura
 ged to dress in Cabaret style attire with fun prizes going to the best dre
 ssed couple and best dressed table. \n\nWe also welcome attendees to join
  us in the morning at either of two optional event additions. Enjoy the be
 auty of Tomales Bay\, learn about oyster farming\, and enjoy a delicious b
 owl of bouillabaisse and other delectables from 8:00 AM – 11:00 AM at M
 arshall\, Tomales Bay.\n\nOption 1:   Self-guided hike\, oyster farm tou
 r\, and brunch on a private beach.\n\nOption 2:  Two hour guided kayak to
 ur by Point Reyes Adventure Company\, oyster farm tour\, and brunch on a p
 rivate beach
LOCATION:Bodega Bay Oyster Company
URL:https://www.sonomamtn.com/event-details/la-fete-zazou
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sonoma County Hot Air Balloon Classic
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260719T040000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260719T103000
UID:2605299inuvTuCz0a6HpVTs4t9Uw
DESCRIPTION:Rise & Shine at the Balloon Festival! \n\nLooking for a magic
 al way to start your day? Join us for an unforgettable two-day Balloon Fes
 tival packed with fun for all ages!\n\n 4 AM Glow Show – Watch the sky
  come alive as glowing balloons flicker like fireflies in the early mornin
 g darkness. It’s a breathtaking sight you won’t want to miss!\n\n FRE
 E Kids Zone – After the glow show\, let the little ones run wild with g
 ames and activities designed just for them.\n\n Food & Vendors – Grab 
 delicious bites\, browse unique merchandise\, and soak in the festive atmo
 sphere while we prepare for potential balloon launches. Weather permitting
 .\n\n Tethered Balloon Rides – Weather permitting\, experience the thr
 ill of rising gently above the ground for a one-of-a-kind view!\n\nBring y
 our friends\, bring your family\, and come create unforgettable memories t
 ogether. Start your morning with wonder\, laughter\, and a sky full of col
 or!\n\n Don’t miss out—plan your visit today!
LOCATION:Sonoma County Event Center at the Fairgrounds
URL:https://www.schabc.org/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:TAKE YOUR TIME: Oil Pintings by Sharon Eisley
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260719T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260719T170000
UID:2605296aykqw093kO4RK5JMspmSQ
DESCRIPTION:“Take Your Time”\n\nChange and transformation take time. I
 n her newest oil paintings Sharon Eisley explores the time as a process. B
 e it moving through grief\, re-framing your story of self\, or birthing so
 me new creation\, each painting lures you in with beautiful application th
 en holds you in time for a closer examination of our human experience. Eis
 ley's paintings are all inspired by tarot cards and her personal journey. 
 Tarot readings will be offered at the reception by @SymbolWarehouse for an
  optional small donation.\n\nOur guest artist\, Robert Benson\, will be ch
 allenging your eyes to fill in the details with his impressionist watercol
 ors.\n\nThis June 20th reception will be the FINAL art opening for Sebasto
 pol Gallery in its home of almost 20 years! This show may last only throug
 h June 2026\, then move to our new location. Or it may be up through June 
 and July. Either way\, this will be your last chance to come celebrate our
  local\, amazing group of artists at 150 N Main St.. “Take Your Time” 
 is a reminder to our collective to take our time finding and setting up ou
 r new home for all of you. I hope you can all come celebrate all the time 
 and art we shared with you in our lovely gallery.\n\nwww.sharoneisley.com
LOCATION:Sebastopol Gallery
URL:http://sebastopolgallery.com
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
