BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:BLS Certification Class (American Heart Association)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260721T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260721T090000
UID:260605PuqInia3UE-qBNSj-C07Hw
DESCRIPTION:BLS Certification Class \\(AHA\\) - In Person\, Instructor-Led
 \n\nAmerican Heart Association BLS certification class \\(in-person\, inst
 ructor-led class in our Rohnert Park classroom\\). BLS \\(Basic Life Suppo
 rt\\) is the required CPR class for healthcare providers. Includes cardiac
  and respiratory arrest management\, CPR\, AED use\, and choking treatment
  for all ages. This class is appropriate for initial BLS or BLS renewal.\n
 \nVive CPR is an American Heart Association \\(AHA\\) Training Site. AHA "
 BLS Provider" certifications are issued on the same day.\n\nWe also offer 
 Blended Learning BLS certification courses \\(online course plus in-person
  Skills Session\\).\n\nLearn from a top-rated\, local CPR training company
  with over 1\,000 5-star reviews! Our classes are fun\, engaging\, and exp
 ertly taught by experienced first responders.\n\nLearn More & Enroll: http
 s://vivecpr.com/class/bls-certification/\n\nQuestions? Call/text \\(707\\)
  612-3277 or https://vivecpr.com/contact
LOCATION:Vive CPR
URL:https://vivecpr.com/class/bls-certification
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tuesdays in the Plaza: Máxima Frecuencia (Latin / Norteño / Corr
 idos)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260721T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260721T200000
UID:260604a8Q6pV9TY06GEr7FeXuSoA
DESCRIPTION:Our weekly summer concerts in the Healdsburg Plaza from 6:00 p
 .m. to 8:00 p.m. provide an eclectic and unique line-up of bands\, and hav
 e been assembled to please a wide array of musical interests. Food vendors
  will be on-hand to offer locally sourced food for sale starting at 5:00 p
 .m. with the music beginning at 6:00 p.m.\n\nAbout the band: Maxima Frecue
 ncia\, a band from Santa Rosa\, CA\, is a prominent figure in the regional
  Mexican music scene. The band is known for its rhythmic melodies and poig
 nant lyrics\, which blend traditional Mexican sounds with modern influence
 s. Their performances are characterized by passionate vocal delivery and u
 pbeat live energy\, creating a lively and expressive atmosphere. The band'
 s flexibility in blending traditional Mexican folk music with contemporary
  production techniques is evident in their music.\n\nMaxima Frecuencia's s
 ongs resonate with listeners\, brimming with passion\, longing\, and resil
 ience. Their lyrical storytelling and heartfelt songs forge a strong bond 
 between the performer and the audience\, making them a beloved figure in t
 he Latin music community. Maxima Frecuencia's influence on the genre is un
 deniable\, with their melodies and compelling narratives leaving a lasting
  impression on the Latin music scene.
LOCATION:Healdsburg Plaza
URL:https://healdsburg.gov/335/Tuesdays-in-the-Plaza
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Summer Teen & Young Adult Group
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260721T161500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260721T173000
UID:260603wHrq1h5l2kWrnyLzt8TCdw
DESCRIPTION:Summer can bring a mix of freedom and uncertainty—more unstr
 uctured time\, shifting routines\, and social pressures that don’t take 
 a break. Our summer groups are designed to offer a supportive space where 
 teens and young adults can stay connected\, build skills\, and feel unders
 tood during this transition.\n\nAt Juniper & Jade Psychotherapy\, we belie
 ve growth happens in connection. These groups provide a safe\, therapist-l
 ed environment where participants can explore their experiences\, strength
 en relationships\, and build confidence in themselves.
LOCATION:Juniper & Jade Psychotherapy Inc
URL:https://juniperandjadepsychotherapy.com/group-therapy
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Valley of the Moon Music Festival: Alfresco Concert 2 at Buena Vis
 ta Winery
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260721T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260721T190000
UID:260603CoVM38X3NE662t7kNETs-g
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy chamber music under warm summer skies at Buena Vista Win
 ery\, one of Sonoma’s most iconic destinations. This relaxed outdoor per
 formance pairs world-class musicians with wine country ambiance in the win
 ery’s scenic courtyard. Wine and light snacks will be available for purc
 hase\, and picnics are welcome. Arrive early to enjoy the grounds before t
 he 7 p.m. performance. Concert duration: approximately 1 hour with no inte
 rmission.\n\nThe Valley of the Moon Music Festival returns July 11–26\, 
 2026\, with Postcards from Dvořák\, a season inspired by the travels\, i
 nfluences\, and cultural connections behind the composer’s music. Set in
  the heart of Sonoma Valley\, the festival brings together internationally
  acclaimed musicians for historically informed performances that blend wor
 ld-class classical music with the beauty and charm of wine country.
LOCATION:Buena Vista Historical Winery
URL:https://valleyofthemoonmusicfestival.org/event/alfresco-concert-2-2/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:TAKE YOUR TIME: Oil Pintings by Sharon Eisley
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260721T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260721T170000
UID:260529H8itQHnnXEap33BEAIintw
DESCRIPTION:“Take Your Time”\n\nChange and transformation take time. I
 n her newest oil paintings Sharon Eisley explores the time as a process. B
 e it moving through grief\, re-framing your story of self\, or birthing so
 me new creation\, each painting lures you in with beautiful application th
 en holds you in time for a closer examination of our human experience. Eis
 ley's paintings are all inspired by tarot cards and her personal journey. 
 Tarot readings will be offered at the reception by @SymbolWarehouse for an
  optional small donation.\n\nOur guest artist\, Robert Benson\, will be ch
 allenging your eyes to fill in the details with his impressionist watercol
 ors.\n\nThis June 20th reception will be the FINAL art opening for Sebasto
 pol Gallery in its home of almost 20 years! This show may last only throug
 h June 2026\, then move to our new location. Or it may be up through June 
 and July. Either way\, this will be your last chance to come celebrate our
  local\, amazing group of artists at 150 N Main St.. “Take Your Time” 
 is a reminder to our collective to take our time finding and setting up ou
 r new home for all of you. I hope you can all come celebrate all the time 
 and art we shared with you in our lovely gallery.\n\nwww.sharoneisley.com
LOCATION:Sebastopol Gallery
URL:http://sebastopolgallery.com
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Creative Arts Camp at Hanna Center
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260721T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260721T160000
