UID:260709_HFvSWN2zUaaxXANiibAZQ
DESCRIPTION:Sit & Stitch is offered the 2nd & 4th Mondays a month from 3:3
 0 to 5:30 pm. For July\, it will be the 13th & the 27th. You can drop in f
 or any amount of time. You may continue needle felting and macrame as we n
 ow have all of the supplies. We also have some people learning how to knit
  and crochet. We will also have tea\, so bring your favorite covered drink
  container. Sit and Stitch is for people to come and work on any fiber art
 s activity that they have while visiting with others. Most people will bri
 ng their own projects\, but we always have hooks\, needles\, and yarn and 
 sometimes we will offer a project with instructions that people may choose
  to make. Let us know what you would like to learn this year. We share ide
 as\, skills\, and encouragement with each other. This summer we will be ad
 ding sewing\, weaving\, and decorative mending to our regular projects of 
 knitting and crocheting. Soon\, we will also have a sewing machine availab
 le for use. Children can come if they are accompanied one to one with an a
 dult.
LOCATION:Guerneville Regional Library
