BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sonoma Sundays on the Plaza - Huney Knuckles
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260802T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260802T170000
UID:260508oos0IWlo7kCZ7NWqCNtkxw
DESCRIPTION:This summer\, Music in Place and the City of Sonoma invite you
  to soak up the sunshine\, sip local wine\, and dance to live music at the
  Sonoma Plaza Grinstead Amphitheater during Sonoma Sundays On the Plaza\, 
 a free concert series running June 7 through October 4\, 2026.\n\nThis wee
 k's lineup features Huney Knuckles! With the left hand keyboard bass wizar
 dry of Kevin Wong along with the indomitable pocket of Darian Gray (tourin
 g drummer for Booker T Jones for the past 14 years)\, the Huney Knuckles a
 re undisputedly known as “the best band in the bay right now”\, elevat
 ed to electrifying heights by the lighting fast solos of virtuoso guitaris
 t Brian Sheu along with the world class musicianship of grammy award winni
 ng saxophonist Tony Peebles. Fusing watertight grooves with high energy sh
 reds that will make you want to jump out of your seat\, this 4-piece instr
 umental powerhouse has made a huge noise in the local scene\, serving up s
 oulful compositions\, mind bending solos\, & insanely funky jams at the hi
 ghest level possible.\n\nSonoma Sundays are free and open to all\, thanks 
 to the generous support of the Sonoma Community Center\, The Dawn Redwoods
  Trust\, and the McNeely Family Foundation.\n\nPack your picnic\, bring yo
 ur dancing shoes\, and meet us on the Plaza!
LOCATION:Grinstead Amphitheater
URL:https://musicinplace.org/event/sonoma-sundays-on-the-plaza-8-2/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jeffrey Halford & The Healers
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260802T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260802T000000
UID:260307zOZyf4-hNkeBQhXIXBlBLA
DESCRIPTION:Of the many marks of genius associated with rock n’ roll gre
 atness\, the knack for surrounding oneself with transformational talent lo
 oms especially large\, with The Rolling Stones being perhaps the most nota
 ble example. Jeffrey Halford treads a poetic rootsy path on his latest rel
 ease\, SOUL CRUSADE\, combining a bulletproof collection of songs inspired
  by gospel\, folk\, soul\, and blues\, with a formidable roster of musical
  contributors. The result is one of Halford’s most approachable and easy
 -grooving.\n\nHis latest album release\, SOUL CRUSADE\, is the follow-up t
 o the critically acclaimed record WEST TOWARDS SOUTH. The album came out i
 n Europe on Continental Song City\, debuted in September at \\#2\, and the
 n undisputedly reached \\#1 in October 2022 and stayed in the chart for fo
 ur months. \n\nJEFFREY HALFORD & THE HEALERS are gearing up for their eigh
 th European tour in September and October 2025\, bringing their signature 
 blend of raw rock ‘n’ roll\, country\, and soul back to the stage. But
  this tour isn’t just another run—it marks the 25th anniversary of KER
 OSENE\, the album \\(release date Friday\, August 29th\, 2025\\) that put 
 Halford on the map as a true Americana troubadour.
LOCATION:The Penngrove Pub
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/107954096?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
